change-id: mylnzmrtzvwwzusstlqttzxtpkuumwrl

Tested on a scratch colocated repo with a second workspace that has
no .git. A series thread piped as one mbox (cover letter, two
patches, a review reply) applied the two patches as two changes
carrying each patch's author and date, and skipped the rest. A
patch that does not apply, or a non-empty @, stopped with nothing
changed. Like git am, the applied changes get new change ids; the
Change-Id header is not carried over.

